{"donor_recipient_matching": "Donor-recipient matching is a critical process in organ transplantation that involves selecting the most compatible donor for a recipient to improve the success rate of the transplant. This process considers various factors such as blood type, tissue type, and other medical criteria to ensure the best possible match.|Here is another description: Donor-recipient matching is a process in organ transplantation where donors and recipients are evaluated for compatibility based on various factors such as blood type, tissue type, and other medical considerations to optimize the success of the transplant."},
