{"anns": "Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs) are a type of AI model that mimics the functional architecture of neurons, with input and output layers. They are used in various applications, including decision-making processes in organ transplantation.|Here is another description: Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs) are a type of AI model that mimics the functional architecture of neurons, with input and output layers. They are designed to handle large databases and can be used for various classification tasks, including donor-recipient matching in organ transplantation.|Here is another description: Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs) are a type of AI model that mimics the functional architecture of neurons, with input and output layers. They can be used with large databases to improve generalizability.|Here is another description: Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs) are a type of AI model that mimics the functional architecture of neurons, with input and output layers. They are used in various applications, including organ transplantation for donor-recipient matching.|Here is another description: ANNs, or artificial neural networks, are a type of machine learning model inspired by the structure and function of the human brain. They consist of layers of interconnected nodes or \"neurons\" that process and transmit information. ANNs are particularly useful in handling complex, multi-variable problems and can generalize well when provided with large datasets, although they are often considered black-box models due to their opaque decision-making processes."},
