{"majority_class_recipient_surviving_graft": "The majority class (recipient/surviving graft) refers to the most common outcome in transplantation scenarios, where both the recipient survives and the graft functions properly. This class is significant in unbalanced datasets where one outcome is much more frequent than the other."},
