{"the_concept_of_correct_classification_rate_ccr_or_accuracy": "The concept of correct classification rate (CCR) or accuracy is a metric used to measure the effectiveness of a classification model. It is defined as the percentage of correctly classified training patterns, providing an indication of how well the model predicts the majority class outcomes."},
