{"first_action": "The first action refers to a step in a process designed to address specific challenges in matching donor-recipient pairs for liver transplants. It is part of a two-step solution aimed at ensuring that the sickest patients are prioritized and that the clinical relevance of numerical probabilities is maintained."},
{"first_action__is_to_apply__ann_ccr_and_ann_ms_algorithms_only_to_candidates_with_the_greatest_urgency": "The predicate \"is to apply\" indicates the action that must be taken as part of the solution. In this context, it means implementing specific algorithms to a selected group of candidates to achieve a desired outcome in the matching process."},
{"ann_ccr_and_ann_ms_algorithms_only_to_candidates_with_the_greatest_urgency": "The object \"ANN-CCR and ANN-MS algorithms only to candidates with the greatest urgency\" describes the specific algorithms (ANN-CCR for predicting graft survival and ANN-MS for predicting graft loss) that are to be applied exclusively to those patients who are in the most critical condition, ensuring that the most urgent cases are given priority."},
{"second_action": "The second action refers to a specific step in a process designed to address the limitations of predictive algorithms in clinical decision-making. It is part of a two-step approach aimed at ensuring that the predictions made by the algorithms are clinically relevant and fair to all patients, especially those in the most urgent need."},
