{"rule_based_system_capable_of_establishing_when_a_survival_probability_difference_and_a_loss_probability_difference_are_relevant": "The object \"rule-based system capable of establishing when a survival probability difference and a loss probability difference are relevant\" describes a system that uses predefined rules to assess the significance of differences in survival and loss probabilities. This system is designed to ensure that the differences in probabilities predicted by the ANN-CCR and ANN-MS models are not only statistically significant but also clinically meaningful, thereby aiding in making more informed and equitable clinical decisions."},
{"rule_based_system": "A rule-based system is a method of decision-making that uses a set of predefined rules to determine the best course of action. In the context of the provided text, the rule-based system is designed to address the limitations of the ANN-CCR and ANN-MS algorithms by establishing when differences in survival and loss probabilities are clinically relevant."},
{"rule_based_system__must_resolve__possible_ties_between_d_r_pairs": "The rule-based system must resolve refers to the necessity for the system to make decisions or judgments in situations where the ANN-CCR and ANN-MS algorithms provide ambiguous or tied results. This involves determining which D-R pair is more favorable based on the established rules."},
