{"ten_fold_randomization": "Ten-fold randomization is a cross-validation technique used in machine learning to evaluate the performance of models. It involves dividing the dataset into ten equal parts, training the model on nine parts, and validating it on the remaining part. This process is repeated ten times, with each part serving as the validation set once, to ensure robust and unbiased model evaluation."},
