{"ability_of_deep_learning_algorithms_to_predict_complications_resulting_in_death_after_liver_transplantation": "The object \"ability of deep-learning algorithms to predict complications resulting in death after liver transplantation\" describes the focus of the assessment. It involves the capability of advanced computational models, specifically deep-learning algorithms, to forecast severe post-operative complications that could lead to patient death following liver transplantation surgery."},
{"deep_learning_algorithms": "Deep-learning algorithms are advanced computational models inspired by the structure and function of the human brain. They are designed to process complex data and make decisions or predictions based on patterns learned from large datasets."},
{"deep_learning_algorithms__predict__complications_resulting_in_death_after_liver_transplantation": "The predicate \"predict\" in this context refers to the capability of deep-learning algorithms to forecast or estimate the likelihood of specific outcomes based on the input data they have been trained on. In medical applications, this often involves anticipating patient outcomes or complications following a procedure."},
{"complications_resulting_in_death_after_liver_transplantation": "Complications resulting in death after liver transplantation refer to severe post-operative issues that lead to patient mortality following a liver transplant. These complications can include graft failure, infections, or other critical conditions that arise after the transplantation procedure."},
