{"a_lower_economic_investment": "A lower economic investment refers to reduced financial costs associated with medical procedures and treatments. In the context of liver transplantation, this would include lower expenses related to ICU stays, re-transplantation needs, and other medical interventions that are necessary when a graft does not function properly."},
{"a_methodology_capable_of_predicting_the_best_performance_of_grafts": "A methodology capable of predicting the best performance of grafts is a system or approach designed to forecast the optimal functioning of organ grafts, particularly in the context of liver transplantation. This methodology aims to enhance decision-making processes by providing accurate predictions that can inform donor-recipient matching and improve patient outcomes."},
{"a_methodology_capable_of_predicting_the_best_performance_of_grafts__reduce__costs": "The predicate \"reduce\" in this context signifies the action of decreasing or minimizing something. Here, it refers to the capability of the methodology to lower certain negative outcomes or expenses associated with liver transplantation, such as the economic investment required due to graft dysfunction or failure."},
{"costs": "Costs in the context of liver transplantation refer to the financial expenditures associated with the procedure and its aftermath. These costs can include hospital stays, ICU care, re-transplantation procedures, and other medical expenses incurred due to graft dysfunction or failure. Reducing these costs would lead to both individual and societal benefits by making the transplantation process more efficient and affordable."},
{"ai_based_algorithms": "AI-based algorithms are advanced computational methods that utilize artificial intelligence to analyze complex data and make predictions or decisions. In the context of organ transplantation, these algorithms aim to improve the decision-making process for donor-recipient matching."},
{"ai_based_algorithms__overcome__mental_barrier_of_the_clinician_to_combine_statistical_metrics_and_models_based_on_deep_learning": "To overcome signifies the need for AI-based algorithms to surmount significant challenges or barriers. In this context, it refers to the necessity for these algorithms to address and resolve the hesitations or resistance clinicians may have towards integrating AI with traditional statistical methods."},
{"mental_barrier_of_the_clinician_to_combine_statistical_metrics_and_models_based_on_deep_learning": "The mental barrier of the clinician to combine statistical metrics and models based on deep learning represents a psychological or conceptual obstacle. Clinicians may be hesitant to adopt AI-driven approaches due to a lack of trust, understanding, or comfort with merging conventional statistical methods with advanced machine learning techniques."},
{"ai_based_models__represent__invaluable_tools_for_decision_making_in_d_r_pairing_and_the_management_of_the_liver_transplantation_waiting_lists": "The predicate \"represent\" in this context signifies that AI-based models are seen as embodying or exemplifying a certain quality or function. Here, it indicates that these models are considered to embody the quality of being invaluable tools."},
{"invaluable_tools_for_decision_making_in_d_r_pairing_and_the_management_of_the_liver_transplantation_waiting_lists": "Invaluable tools for decision-making in D-R pairing and the management of the liver transplantation waiting lists are resources or systems that provide critical support and enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of decision processes. These tools are essential in matching donors with recipients and managing transplantation waiting lists, ultimately aiming to improve patient outcomes and resource utilization."},
