{"d_r_matching": "D-R matching, or Donor-Recipient matching, is a critical process in organ transplantation that involves pairing compatible donors with recipients to maximize transplant success and minimize rejection risks. This process considers various factors such as blood type, tissue type, and other medical criteria. AI models are increasingly utilized to enhance the predictability and effectiveness of this matching process."},
