{"artificial_neural_networks_ann_and_random_forest_rf": "Artificial neural networks (ANN) and random forest (RF) are two types of AI models used in donor-recipient matching. ANNs mimic the functional architecture of neurons and are effective with large databases, though they are sensitive to data quality and act as black-box models. RF builds decision trees, works well with small cohorts, and can select top variables, but is less practical with large databases due to the number of decision trees generated."},
