{"ann__mimics__the_functional_architecture_of_neurons": "The term \"mimics\" in this context refers to how ANNs are designed to emulate or replicate the operational and structural aspects of biological neurons. This involves creating input and output layers within the network to process information similarly to how neurons function in the human brain."},
{"the_functional_architecture_of_neurons": "The functional architecture of neurons refers to the way neurons in the human brain are structured and operate, including the transmission of signals through input and output layers. ANNs are designed to replicate this architecture to process and analyze complex data."},
