{"results_of_liver_transplantation": "The results of liver transplantation refer to the outcomes and success rates associated with the surgical procedure of replacing a diseased liver with a healthy one from a donor."},
{"results_of_liver_transplantation__have_improved_considerably__due_to_the_advances_in_surgical_technique_the_management_of_immunosuppressive_drugs_the_better_knowledge_of_post_transplant_long_term_morbidities_and_the_greater_knowledge_of_the_mechanisms_involved_in_the_preservation_of_the_organ": "The phrase \"have improved considerably\" indicates a significant enhancement or progress in the outcomes of liver transplantation over time, attributed to various advancements and better understandings in the field."},
{"due_to_the_advances_in_surgical_technique_the_management_of_immunosuppressive_drugs_the_better_knowledge_of_post_transplant_long_term_morbidities_and_the_greater_knowledge_of_the_mechanisms_involved_in_the_preservation_of_the_organ": "The improvements in liver transplantation results are due to multiple factors including advances in surgical techniques, better management of immunosuppressive drugs, enhanced knowledge of long-term post-transplant complications, and a deeper understanding of the mechanisms involved in organ preservation."},
{"recipient_and_graft_survivals": "Recipient and graft survivals refer to the rates at which both the recipients of liver transplants and the transplanted livers themselves continue to function and remain viable post-operation."},
{"recipient_and_graft_survivals__are_around__95_in_1_year": "The phrase \"are around\" indicates an approximate value or range, suggesting that the survival rates are close to, but not exactly, the specified percentage."},
{"95_in_1_year": "95% in 1 year signifies a high rate of survival for both recipients and grafts within the first year following a liver transplantation, reflecting the effectiveness of current medical practices and technologies in this field."},
