{"current_approaches": "Current approaches refer to the existing methods and strategies employed in the field of organ transplantation, including the expansion of inclusion criteria for candidates and the implementation of transplant oncology."},
{"current_approaches__aggravate__the_problem": "Aggravate in this context means to make a problem worse or more severe. The current approaches are described as exacerbating the existing issues in organ transplantation."},
{"the_problem": "The problem here refers to the disproportion between the number of organ donors and the growing demand for transplantation, which is compounded by long waiting lists and high mortality rates among candidates awaiting donor organs."},
{"countries_with_deceased_donor_rates_of_20_30_pmp": "Countries with deceased donor rates of 20-30 per million population (pmp) are nations where the number of deceased organ donors falls within this specific range per million inhabitants."},
{"countries_with_deceased_donor_rates_of_20_30_pmp__present_utilization_of__close_to_100": "Present utilization of indicates the current rate at which available resources, in this case, deceased donor organs, are being used or applied within a given context."},
{"close_to_100": "Close to 100% utilization means that nearly all available deceased donor organs are being used, indicating a high efficiency in the use of these resources within the specified countries."},
