{"prediction_of_the_model": "The prediction of the model refers to the anticipated outcomes or results generated by a statistical or machine learning model based on the input data provided. In this context, it specifically pertains to the model's ability to forecast the survival of the recipient and the graft in the short and medium term."},
{"prediction_of_the_model__would_not_be__reliable": "The phrase \"would not be\" indicates a conditional statement where the reliability of the model's prediction is contingent upon certain conditions being met. In this case, it suggests that if variables with a high percentage of missing values are not eliminated, the model's predictions will lack reliability."},
{"reliable": "Reliability in this context means the consistency and accuracy of the model's predictions. A reliable model would produce consistent and accurate results, which are crucial for making informed decisions regarding donor-recipient matching and predicting outcomes like recipient and graft survival."},
{"database__is_divided_into__two_groups": "The database is divided into two groups to facilitate the training and testing of a predictive model. This division allows for the assessment of the model's performance on unseen data, ensuring its generalizability and reliability."},
