{"training_group": "The training group refers to a subset of data used to train a predictive model. In this context, it is specifically designated to include 75% of the donor-recipient (D-R) pairs from the preprocessed database."},
{"training_group__is__75_of_the_d_r_pairs": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies the allocation or assignment of a specific proportion of D-R pairs to the training group. It indicates that the training group comprises a certain percentage of the total D-R pairs available in the database."},
{"75_of_the_d_r_pairs": "75% of the D-R pairs represents the portion of the total donor-recipient pairs that are assigned to the training group. This percentage is crucial for ensuring that the model has sufficient data to learn from, while also leaving an adequate amount of data for testing and validation purposes."},
{"testing_group": "The testing group refers to a subset of data used to evaluate the performance and accuracy of a predictive model. In this context, it is specifically 25% of the donor-recipient (D-R) pairs that are set aside for this purpose."},
{"testing_group__is__25_of_the_d_r_pairs": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies the allocation or designation of a specific portion of the D-R pairs to the testing group. It indicates that 25% of the total D-R pairs have been earmarked for testing the model's predictions."},
{"25_of_the_d_r_pairs": "The object \"25% of the D-R pairs\" refers to the proportion of donor-recipient pairs that are allocated to the testing group. This subset is used to assess how well the predictive model performs on unseen data, ensuring that the model's predictions are reliable and accurate."},
{"percentages": "The percentages refer to the division of data into training and testing groups, which are crucial for the development and validation of predictive models. These percentages are adjustable based on the specific requirements of the analysis."},
