{"model__tries_to_maximize__probability_that_a_d_r_pair_belongs_to_the_surviving_class": "The predicate \"tries to maximize\" indicates the model's objective function, which is to increase the likelihood or probability of a specific outcome. In this context, it aims to enhance the chances that a given D-R pair will fall into the'surviving' class, thereby predicting a successful transplantation outcome."},
{"probability_that_a_d_r_pair_belongs_to_the_surviving_class": "The object \"probability that a D-R pair belongs to the'surviving' class\" refers to the likelihood calculated by the model that a particular combination of donor and recipient will result in a successful transplantation, where the graft survives. This probability is a critical output of the model, informing clinical decisions and predictions about patient outcomes."},
