{"d_r_pair__obtains__probability_of_successful_outcome_ann_ccr_and_of_loss_ann_ms": "The predicate \"obtains\" in this context means that for each donor-recipient pair, certain probabilities are calculated or derived using specific algorithms."},
{"probability_of_successful_outcome_ann_ccr_and_of_loss_ann_ms": "The object \"probability of successful outcome (ANN-CCR) and of loss (ANN-MS)\" refers to the calculated likelihoods of a positive transplant outcome and the risk of graft loss, respectively, using artificial neural network models designated as ANN-CCR for successful outcomes and ANN-MS for losses."},
{"model__would_always_choose__the_pair_with_the_highest_numerical_probability_of_surviving_and_the_lowest_numerical_probability_of_being_lost": "The model's decision-making process involves always selecting the D-R pair that has the highest numerical probability of surviving and the lowest numerical probability of being lost, based on the predictions from the ANN-CCR and ANN-MS algorithms."},
