{"multicenter_study": "A multicenter study refers to a research project conducted across multiple centers or institutions, often involving a large number of participants to enhance the generalizability of the findings. In this context, the multicenter study was performed across 11 Spanish liver transplant units.|Here is another description: A multicenter study is a research study conducted across multiple medical centers or institutions. This particular study was designed to evaluate the effectiveness of certain models in predicting graft survival in liver transplantations."},
