{"the_presence_of_a_considerable_percentage_of_missing_values_for_many_relevant_variables_in_the_unos_database": "The object describes the specific issue affecting the UNOS database, which is the presence of a significant percentage of missing values for many relevant variables. This data quality issue is identified as the primary reason for the differences in model performance compared to previous studies."},
{"after_removing_all_variables_with_missing_values_10": "The process of removing all variables with missing values greater than 10% from a dataset, likely in the context of predictive modeling or statistical analysis."},
{"after_removing_all_variables_with_missing_values_10__only__28_variables_remained_in_the_model": "The action or result of applying a specific threshold (in this case, 10% missing values) to filter out variables from a dataset, leading to a reduced set of variables that meet the criteria."},
{"28_variables_remained_in_the_model": "The remaining set of 28 variables in the model after the removal of variables with more than 10% missing values, indicating the variables that were considered reliable or complete enough to be included in further analysis or modeling."},
{"the_disadvantage_of_ai_models_with_the_unos_database": "The disadvantage of AI models with the UNOS database refers to the challenges faced by artificial intelligence models when utilizing the United Network for Organ Sharing (UNOS) database for predictive analytics. This includes issues such as a considerable percentage of missing values for many relevant variables, which limits the effectiveness of the models."},
{"the_disadvantage_of_ai_models_with_the_unos_database__has_also_been_found_for_the_same_reasons_in__heart_transplantation": "The phrase \"has also been found for the same reasons in\" indicates a relationship where a particular issue or finding observed in one context (AI models with the UNOS database) is also applicable or evident in another context (heart transplantation) due to similar underlying reasons, such as data quality issues."},
{"heart_transplantation": "Heart transplantation in this context refers to the medical procedure of transplanting a heart from a donor to a recipient, often studied using large databases like UNOS for outcomes and predictive modeling. The challenges faced by AI models with the UNOS database are also applicable here due to similar data quality issues."},
