{"ann__stands_for__artificial_neural_networks": "\"Stands for\" is a relational term indicating that ANN is an abbreviation or acronym representing a longer, more descriptive term. In this context, it clarifies the full meaning behind the acronym ANN, which is commonly used in technical and scientific literature."},
{"meld__stands_for__model_for_end_stage_liver_disease": "The phrase \"stands for\" indicates that MELD is an abbreviation or shorthand representation of a longer, more descriptive term related to liver disease."},
{"model_for_end_stage_liver_disease": "The model for end-stage liver disease (MELD) is a scoring system used to assess the severity of liver disease, particularly in patients awaiting liver transplantation, and is crucial in determining the urgency of transplantation."},
{"d_meld": "D-MELD is a composite metric used in the context of liver transplantation to assess donor suitability and predict post-transplant outcomes. It is specifically mentioned in the context of validating artificial neural network methodologies in an external database."},
{"d_meld__stands_for__donor_age_and_meld_score": "\"Stands for\" indicates that D-MELD is an abbreviation or acronym representing a specific combination of factors. In this case, it represents the combination of donor age and MELD score, which are critical factors in evaluating donor risk and transplant success."},
{"donor_age_and_meld_score": "Donor age and MELD score are individual components that, when combined, form the D-MELD score. Donor age refers to the age of the liver donor, which can impact the quality and functionality of the transplanted organ. The MELD (Model for End-Stage Liver Disease) score is a numerical scale used to assess the severity of liver disease in patients awaiting a liver transplant."},
{"dri": "DRI, as mentioned in the context, is an abbreviation used in the field of liver transplantation to denote a specific index."},
{"dri__stands_for__donor_risk_index": "The predicate \"stands for\" indicates that DRI is an acronym or abbreviation that represents a longer term or phrase, in this case, related to liver transplantation metrics."},
{"donor_risk_index": "Donor Risk Index (DRI) is a scoring system used to assess the quality of a donor liver, which is crucial in predicting post-transplant outcomes and survival rates for recipients."},
